Z||000000||fierospeeder||10-30-2001||10:17 PM||||Im going to be buying a pressure washer, to clean up my concrete before i put my paint down. <P>I already put two layers of resurfacing concrete.  It seems that the etcher rises up to the surface, and i think some of the oil also surfaced.  The concrete is sticking very well to the surface so i have no worries about that.<P><BR>To rent a washer, its 35 bucks for 2 hours and 80 for the whole day.   I saw some affordable washers that i can buy.  I was wondering should i get an electric or a gas pressure washer?<P>the electric is 3hp and makes 1750psi 1.8gpm<BR>the gas is 3.5hp and makes more then 2000psi at 2.- gpm.<P>Im also going to be using it to clean car related things too.  Suggestions would be great.||||reg||1
